You may sell your independently created hardware, software, reports,
analyses and other outputs. You keep your rights in your own work.

An "Independent Product" has substantial functionality and value beyond
the Utilities and is not an offering of the Utilities themselves. It may
incorporate the Utilities as an incidental supporting component, provided
customers are not offered the Utilities, or their material functionality,
as a standalone tool, separately marketed feature, or reusable service
for the customers' own workflows. This permission includes distributing
such a component within an otherwise qualifying paid Independent Product.

Renaming a Utility, changing its interface, adding an AI or API wrapper,
hosting it, or making only minor changes does not, by itself, create an
Independent Product. Section 4 controls an offering that falls within
its restrictions even if the offering includes additional software.

You may charge for genuine consulting, engineering, training, integration
or support work that uses the Utilities, provided the charge is for your
